2. STATEMENT OF CHANGES  (GNU GPL-3.0 section 5a, incorporated by LGPL-3.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is a MODIFIED work. It is not iChun's Morph and must not be mistaken for
it.

WHAT CHANGED, and WHEN:

  * July 2026 — the mod was rewritten for **Minecraft 26.2 on the Fabric mod
    loader**. The original targets Minecraft 1.6.4 on Minecraft Forge. No
    upstream source file survives verbatim: the original's Forge-era classes
    (`morph.*`) have no counterpart in modern Minecraft, so every file in this
    repository is newly written.

  * September 2026 — the same sources also build for **Minecraft 26.3** on
    Fabric. A per-version build layer (`versions/`, see `versions/README.md`)
    derives the 26.3 jar from the 26.2 sources; the handful of calls whose
    shape differs between the two versions are isolated in small
    per-version classes.

  * What is DERIVED from the original, and is therefore covered by LGPL-3.0,
    is the substance rather than the text: the morph identity model (entity
    type plus normalised variant NBT) and its "same identity replaces in
    place / new variant appends" acquisition rule, the ~4-second transition
    and the three morph rules that guard it, the twelve passive abilities and
    their per-player tick/apply/kill lifecycle, the hostile target-cancel
    modes, the hitbox / eye-height / camera adoption, player morphs and their
    per-username selector grouping, the four selector sort modes and the
    selector's scroll cadence, the ability-icon set, the `/morph` command
    tree, the hurt-sound swap, the flight-exhaustion arithmetic, the
    demorph-on-death modes, the volatile-NBT strip, and the configuration
    options with their defaults. These were transcribed from the upstream
    source named in section 1 and from a decompile of the released 0.7.1 jar.

  * One user-visible string is reproduced verbatim — the refusal message
    "You may not rest now, you are in morph" — because for a message the
    wording *is* the behaviour. Everything else was re-expressed.

  * The artwork and the sounds are iChun's, reused unmodified — see section 4.

  * The port DEVIATES from the original in a number of places, deliberately
    and on the record. Among them: an unloadable morph stays dormant instead
    of silently becoming a Pig; the original's `morph_backup.dat` rotation is
    not reproduced (the modern save path makes it unnecessary); the hardcoded
    per-mob-class ability table is replaced by generic derivation from the
    entity's own properties, so modded mobs behave sensibly without a support
    file; the original API's reflection trampoline is not reproduced; the
    `canSleepMorphed` default is flipped; and re-acquiring a morph you already
    own deliberately does not refresh it in place. Behaviour, appearance and
    configuration therefore do not match the original one-for-one. This is a
    revival, not a faithful reproduction.

  * Development of this port is ongoing; it has not reached a 1.0 release.


